rix is analysed** (this is a study about forking paths); experiment-repo accepts or amends them in `experiment-repo`#4 before analysis, a\n| C7 | **Beyond the real matrix.** To the extent its validation checks pass, do gap and coverage curves extend to n > 300 and larger K? | Split-half prediction, within-support extrapolation (fit K≤75, n≤100 → K=150, n=200), mis-specification sweep. | Fig 6 / appendix |\n| C8 | **Real tool.** Does the gap of a real search tool (DSPy-style) at the same n and budget fall within the replay searchers' predictive interval? | Short arm; ≥20–30 S draws required for \"tested\", otherwise reported as an illustration and the criterion as **not tested**. | Tab 3 |\n**Venue: NeurIPS 2026 main track (venue-repo): 9 content pages including all figures and tables; references, appendix and the mandatory 16-item checklist are outside the limit; double blind.** Floats take at most ≈2 of the 9 pages: Fig 1–5 (each ≈2.3 in high at 5.5 in width) + Tab 1–2 in the main te\n8. **Checklist, reproducibility** (venue's checklist is filled by report from owners' facts).\n- **Fig 6 (C7) — semi-synthetic.** Validation checks (predicted vs real) and extrapolated curves to n>300/large K, marked outside the validated support. May go to the appendix if the checks fail.\n- **Tab 3 (real tool).** Real-tool gap vs replay interval, number of draws, status (tested / illustration).\n- **venue-repo:** answered (NeurIPS 2026, 9 pages).\n- Venue chosen: NeurIPS 2026 (above).\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "d95b3d20-0868-52ba-b261-2528e89504bc", "at": 1795645738.104956, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 11553, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "venue-repo", "actor": "venue-repo", "execution_id": "57e90e3bf2ce5410c2c0365a169ecb25", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "31028589-9ff5-5f4a-b9fc-65d1fdb42113", "at": 17